# 8th Grade Assessment Dashboard: Power BI + SQL + Python

**Status:** Production (in use by 8th grade team) | **Impact:** 45 min/day time savings | **Accuracy:** ±1 point prediction

---

## Problem Statement (Situation)
Manual Excel analysis of 30+ student assessment records (Blue/White tests, Benchmark, 7th STAAR) required 2 hours/planning period. Special populations (30-40% of students with 504/SPED/Dyslexia/EL/At-Risk codes) made tracking accommodations and growth trends nearly impossible for teachers.

## Technical Challenge (Task)
Build a real-time, filterable dashboard that:
- Handles multiple assessment types with inconsistent naming
- Supports class-level AND individual student views
- Predicts future STAAR performance without overfitting
- Runs on existing school infrastructure (Excel exports + district laptops)

## My Solution (Action - Technical)

### 1. Data Pipeline (SQL + Power Query)
```sql
-- Sample: Standardized assessment names across six weeks
SELECT 
    student_id,
    CASE 
        WHEN test_name LIKE '%White%' THEN 'End-of-Six Weeks'
        WHEN test_name LIKE '%Blue%' THEN 'Mid-Six Weeks'
    END as test_type,
    score
FROM raw_assessments
WHERE score IS NOT NULL
